<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tour Magne</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tour Magne is a tower on Mont Cavalier, the highest point of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nimes">Nîmes</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. A pre-Roman stone tower built by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volcae">Volcae</a> Arecomici was enlarged under Augustus into a tall polygonal tower forming part of the Roman walls of Nemausus. About 32 metres high today, it is the largest surviving part of those walls.</p></div>
